    "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions and are mathematically correct. q-69751: substituting x=3,1,-5 after clearing denominators gives coefficients 3,-2,-1. q-120161: r=9 describes the origin-centered circle of radius 9, shown in option 3. q-40791: the displayed origin-centered circle has radius 6, so r=6. q-86947: the positive y-axis has angle π/2, giving (3.5,π/2). q-17150 and q-120186: the radii are √(6²+4²)=√52 and √(1²+(-1)²)=√2. q-8331: swapping coordinates preserves scalar multiplication and vector addition, so all three statements hold. q-120543: the magnitude is √(1+0+9)=√10. q-70425: a+2b=(4,7,-6), whose magnitude is √101. q-18975: dividing (-2,8,3) by √77 produces the stated parallel unit vector. q-101022: AB=(0,-2,4), and division by 2√5 gives the stated unit vector. The negatives of these unit vectors would also be parallel, but neither appears among the current choices. q-43617: 1+tan²θ=sec²θ makes the ratio 1. q-142764: factoring secθ gives secθ(tan²θ+1)=sec³θ. q-142822: expansion gives sec²x+1=2+tan²x. q-142839: the numerator is -tan²x, so the quotient is -tan x. q-120631: the denominator is sin²x sec²x=tan²x, giving cot²x. These trigonometric equalities hold on the original expressions' domains. The q-120631 solution contains an intermediate variable typo, writing tan θ=sin x/cos x; the correct identity uses tan x. Its final answer remains correct. No submitted grades or earlier answers are supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematical verification.",
